#: includes/views/help-tab.php:77
msgid "Set your delivery window"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:78
msgid "On the Delivery tab, enter the minimum and maximum days a parcel takes to arrive after you hand it to the carrier. Set both to the same number for a single date instead of a range. Use 0 for same-day delivery."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:81
msgid "Set your order cutoff"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:82
msgid "Orders placed before this time go out the same day. Anything after it moves to the next dispatch day."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:85
msgid "Tick your non-dispatch days"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:86
msgid "The weekdays you do not send orders out, usually Saturday and Sunday. They are never counted toward the estimate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:89
msgid "Add your holidays"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:90
msgid "Single dates or date ranges you are closed. Tick \"Repeats every year\" for fixed holidays such as Christmas."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:93
msgid "Choose where it appears"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:94
msgid "The Display tab controls product pages, shop archives, cart, and checkout. The Style tab controls wording and colours. The live preview updates as you type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:105
msgid "How the date is worked out"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:108
msgid "QuickShipD keeps the day you dispatch separate from the days a parcel spends in transit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:113
msgid "Start from today"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:114
msgid "If the cutoff time has already passed, move to tomorrow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:118
msgid "Find the dispatch day"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:119
msgid "If that day is a non-dispatch day or a holiday, roll forward until it is not."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:123
msgid "Count the transit days"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:124
msgid "Count forward from the dispatch day, skipping non-dispatch days and holidays."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:129
#: includes/views/help-tab.php:198
msgid "Worked example"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:130
msgid "Weekends off, delivery 1 to 2 days, a customer orders on Saturday. Nothing ships at the weekend, so the dispatch day rolls to Monday. One to two days after Monday gives Tuesday to Wednesday. Monday is never shown as the arrival date, because that is the day the parcel leaves you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:133
msgid "The countdown is hidden on days you do not dispatch, because beating the cutoff on those days cannot change the date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:142
msgid "Same-day dispatch and delivery"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:145
msgid "Delivery days are counted after dispatch, so 0 days means the parcel arrives on the day it goes out. Set the minimum to 0 and the cutoff becomes your same-day deadline."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:147
msgid "Pick your numbers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:152
msgid "What you promise"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:153
msgid "Minimum"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:154
msgid "Maximum"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:159
msgid "Always same day"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:164
msgid "Same day, sometimes next day"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:169
msgid "Next day at the earliest"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:176
msgid "Set it up"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:180
msgid "Set minimum delivery days to 0"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:181
msgid "On the Delivery tab. Set the maximum to 0 as well for a single date, or to 1 if a late order might slip to tomorrow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:184
msgid "Set the cutoff to your last dispatch run"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:185
msgid "This is the moment same-day stops being possible. If your courier collects at 11am, set 11:00. Orders after it automatically move to the next dispatch day, so you never promise a delivery you cannot make."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:188
msgid "Match the non-dispatch days to your opening days"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:189
msgid "Delivering seven days a week? Untick every day. Closed at weekends? Leave Saturday and Sunday ticked, and weekend orders will quote the next working day instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:192
msgid "Say so in the wording"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:193
msgid "On the Style tab, a countdown line such as \"Order within {countdown} for delivery today\" turns the cutoff into a reason to buy now. Keep the countdown switched on for this."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:199
msgid "Minimum 0, maximum 0, cutoff 11:00, closed at weekends. An order at 10:30 on Monday shows Monday, with 30 minutes left on the countdown. At 11:30 the same order shows Tuesday and the countdown disappears. An order on Saturday shows Monday, because nothing is dispatched at the weekend."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:202
msgid "Same-day can also be set for one product only, or for one shipping method such as local delivery, using the overrides described in the Overrides section."
msgstr ""

