msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:387
msgid "Edit a product, open the Shipping tab in Product data, and set its own minimum and maximum days. You can also switch QuickShipD off for that product entirely."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:390
msgid "2. Per shipping method"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:391
msgid "In WooCommerce, Settings, Shipping, open a zone and edit a method. Each method has its own minimum and maximum, so express can quote a faster date than standard. Leave blank to use the store default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:406
msgid "It does not show on my product page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:407
msgid "Check the product is in stock and that QuickShipD is not switched off on it. If the page is built with Elementor, Divi, or another builder, the theme never fires the WooCommerce hook, so drop the [quickshipd] shortcode into the layout where you want it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:411
msgid "The dates on my site do not match the preview"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:412
msgid "Both use your WordPress timezone from Settings, General. If they still differ, a page cache is most likely serving an older copy of the page. Clear it and check again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:416
msgid "The countdown is missing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:417
msgid "The countdown only appears on product pages, only when it is switched on, and only before the cutoff on a day you actually dispatch. After the cutoff there is nothing left to count down to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:421
msgid "Changing shipping method did not change the date"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:422
msgid "Method overrides only apply at cart and checkout, where a method has actually been chosen. Product pages always use the store default, since no method is selected yet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:426
msgid "My estimates moved a day later after updating"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:427
msgid "That is the dispatch day fix in 1.0.5 and it is working as intended. Before it, an order arriving on a day you do not dispatch counted your next working day as a delivery day, which quoted a date you could not meet. Counting now starts after dispatch. If you want the old, shorter quote back, lower the minimum delivery days by one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:431
msgid "It is printing on my packing slips or PDF invoices"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:432
msgid "PDF invoice and packing slip plugins read the order line meta directly, so unticking an email does not remove it from a printed slip. Switch off \"Save on the order\" under Display, Orders & Emails to stop storing it altogether, or use the quickshipd_save_order_item_date filter to skip it for specific orders. Existing orders keep whatever they were given at checkout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:436
msgid "The estimate is missing from order emails"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:437
msgid "Check Display, Orders & Emails. \"Save on the order\" must be on, and the email in question must still be ticked. Only orders placed while the setting was on carry the estimate, so older orders will not gain one retroactively."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:441
msgid "A holiday is not being skipped"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:442
msgid "Add the whole period as one range rather than a line per day, and tick \"Repeats every year\" if you close on the same dates annually. A range has to stay inside one calendar year, so a Christmas to New Year closure needs two entries. The live preview reflects holidays immediately, so use it to confirm the dates land where you expect."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:446
msgid "The plugin is not in my language"
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:447
msgid "Every string is translatable and translations are hosted on translate.wordpress.org. If your language is incomplete, you can submit strings there and WordPress will pull them in automatically once approved. Anything you type yourself, such as the message templates on the Style tab, is shown exactly as you wrote it and is never translated."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:460
msgid "Two filters cover the order record, for cases the settings above do not."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:466
msgid "Return false to keep the estimate off an order line entirely. Receives the line item and the cart item data, so it can be decided per product or per order."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:470
msgid "Return false to hide the estimate in one email. Receives the WooCommerce email id, for example customer_processing_order."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:486
msgid "Dates are worked out in PHP on page load. No external services are contacted and no customer data leaves your site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:487
msgid "Frontend CSS and JavaScript load only on pages that actually show an estimate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:488
msgid "Compatible with HPOS and the block cart and checkout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/views/help-tab.php:489
msgid "Restore Defaults at the bottom of this page resets every setting, including holidays and non-dispatch days."
msgstr ""

#. translators: link to WooCommerce plugin page
#: quickshipd.php:118
#, php-format
msgid "<strong>QuickShipD</strong> requires WooCommerce to be installed and activated. <a href=\"%s\">Install WooCommerce</a>."
msgstr ""
